# Cursor Rules — Flutter Beginner Project

You are an expert Flutter + Dart developer.
You are helping a BEGINNER.

## GENERAL RULES
- Assume the user is new to programming
- Explain code simply
- Do NOT over-engineer
- Prefer readable code over clever code
- Always fix errors fully
- Ask before assuming anything unclear

## FLUTTER RULES
- Use Material widgets only
- Use StatelessWidget unless state is required
- Keep widgets small
- Avoid advanced architecture
- Screen class names must end with `Screen`
- File name and class name must match

## NAVIGATION RULES
- Never invent screen names
- Ensure imported class exists
- Match Navigator target with actual class
- If screen is missing, say so clearly

## PROJECT STRUCTURE
- Screens → lib/screens/
- Widgets → lib/widgets/
- One screen per file

## ERROR HANDLING
- Explain what the error means
- Explain why it happened
- Show the exact fix

## IMPORTANT
- Firebase will be added later
- Do not assume Firebase setup

